__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/RESUME.md

# Derived legacy-corpus manifests: regeneratable via legacy/classify.py,
# but contain full filesystem paths from outside this repo that reveal
# unrelated private project names/structure. Excluded from tracking for
# public release safety -- see legacy/DECISION_PACKET.md.
legacy/manifests/*.json

# foundation/cron_pulse.py's real, live, hourly output on this machine --
# machine-local runtime state/receipts, not source. Regenerates on its
# own; a fresh clone correctly reports these logs as "never fired yet"
# (foundation/sentinel.py::read_pulse_continuity(),
# foundation/mouth_common.py::read_mouth_log_continuity()) until its own
# cron entry runs.
foundation/pulse_log.jsonl
foundation/mouth_*_log.jsonl
foundation/mouth_*_state.json
foundation/dependency_pressure_log.jsonl
foundation/cron_pulse.err.log

# foundation/authority_pulse.py's real default targets -- same
# machine-local runtime-state reasoning as above. Empty/absent on a
# fresh checkout means "no release has ever been issued here," which is
# the deliberately safe, inert default -- see authority_pulse.py's own
# docstring.
foundation/authority_ledger.jsonl
foundation/authority_runtime_tick_log.jsonl

# foundation/autonomy_loop.py's kill switch and receipt log -- same
# machine-local runtime-state reasoning as above. The kill switch must
# never be tracked (dropping it to stop the loop must never itself
# require a commit or dirty the tree the loop's own fail-closed check
# inspects), and the receipt log would otherwise make every cycle after
# the first look like a dirty working tree to the very check meant to
# catch real ambiguity.
.autonomy_stop
foundation/autonomy_loop_log.jsonl
foundation/outcome_ledger.jsonl

# Python build artifacts. Distributions are attached to GitHub Releases,
# never committed -- a build output in git is a second source of truth for
# something `python3 -m pip wheel .` reproduces from the tagged source.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# foundation/operator_cli.py's operator profile -- the real operator's
# own business data (staff count, certifications, insurance, referees).
# Never tracked; operator_profile.example.json documents every field
# and ships with the real current placeholder values.
/operator_profile.json

# Runtime state written by the hunt loop and the scheduled brief. Same
# class as every other ledger above: machine-specific, regenerated on
# demand, and a source of the exact "green on my machine, red in CI"
# failure this repository spent eight commits diagnosing.
foundation/hunt_loop_log.jsonl
foundation/scheduled_brief_log.jsonl
foundation/scheduled_brief_cron.log
briefs/
foundation/deal_pipeline_log.jsonl

# Telegram digest dry-run output (never commit; may echo message content)
digest_out/
*.telegram_creds
